From 934e4bc2948ebf58b06eec4add078fd5c3e8bb57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 05:50:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] P6 round one: OP_TAILCALL, the member-store receiver fix, the
 regen door's ordering

the member-store fix (found by delta blue's pub-fields rewrite):
obj.field = <call-shaped rhs> died with 'only instances and classes
have assignable members' - the assignment's staged receiver temp sat
inside the call rhs's callee register window and was null-filled
before the store read it. the subscript lane had the discipline
(fresh rhs temp above the staging); the member lane now shares it.

OP_TAILCALL / OP_TAILCALL_LONG: 'return name(args);' where the callee
is a plain identifier (register/upvalue/global, no spread) hands the
frame to the callee in place - close upvalues, drop this frame's
handler records, move the staged window down, replace the frame with
the ORIGINAL return contract inherited. one million mutual tailcalls
ride one frame slot. the defer epilogue runs in bytecode before the
handover (the compiler emits it exactly like the classic return).
non-closure callees degrade through the vm_call lane: call_value,
nested run_until under a yield barrier when a frame was pushed, then
the result answers the contract. v1 scope: method/super invokes,
spreads, field/static and lambda callees keep the classic shape.

the regen door's ordering: crosscheck.sh wrote the manifest before
the pins, so a seed that just joined the corpus tripped the manifest
walk's own load-time verification - the door tripped on its fresh
seed. order is now healer, pins, manifest.

new: tests/e2e classes/member_store_call_rhs.ok,
functions/tailcalls.ok, fuzz corpus tailcalls.ok (17 seeds pinned).

gates: builds 9/9, e2e 605x7 (603 -> 605), unit+embed 5x3, capi
334x5, cli 10/10, fuzz x2 gcc==asan (50047 diagnostics, 0 unlocated
- the new seed's mutations), delta blue flat at the pub-fields
baseline (1.40654e7, ~1.35x/1.32x wren)
